  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves creating a star schema-based database to support sales operations in an organization. The system is intended to efficiently manage customer, employee, and product information, as well as track sales transactions.\n\nObjectives\n\n- Develop a structured relational database to store and manage sales-related data.\n- Ensure robust linkage between customers, employees, products, and sales transactions.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Database Administrators: Responsible for managing and maintaining the database.\n- Sales Managers: Utilize the information for tracking sales performance.\n- Employees: Sales staff who input transaction data.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Customer Management: \n   - Store customer details including first name, middle initial, and last name.\n\n2. Employee Management:\n   - Maintain records of employees, capturing personal identification details. \n\n3. Product Catalog:\n   - Maintain a registry of products, including names and prices.\n\n4. Sales Transactions:\n   - Record sales transactions capturing the sales person, customer, product, and quantity details.\n   - Ensure integrity through foreign key relationships among employees, customers, products, and sales entries.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Integrity: Enforce data consistency using foreign key constraints to manage relationships and cascading updates/deletions.\n- Scalability: Design the schema to handle increasing amounts of sales data as the organization grows.\n- Performance: Optimize for quick retrieval of sales and customer information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0126\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_initial` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_initial` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales` (\n  `sales_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
